<title>GERMANY: Schaeuble says French deficit could be problem.</title>
<headline>Schaeuble says French deficit could be problem.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wolfgang Schaeuble, a senior aide to Chancellor Helmut Kohl, said on Wednesday that it could pose a problem for economic and monetary union (EMU) if France's budget deficit was 3.6 percent of gross domestic product in 1997.</p>
<p>Speaking in an interview with ZDF television to be broadcast later today, Schaeuble added that Germany's budget deficit this year could exceed public investment, which is not allowed by the constitution.</p>
</text>
